  "_note": "Inclusion policy (#97 stage 4). Category and inclusion decisions are our own judgment, not sourced from Mojang, so they're kept separate from the upstream snapshot. The representative color's source of truth is the texture's average color; `color` is written here only when the average color can't be derived (omit it when it can). The Japanese name's source of truth is the official ja_JP.lang; `nameJa` is written here only to fill in legacy blocks that can't be looked up via tile.<id>.name (omit it when it can). Setting `included` to false removes an entry from the catalog without discarding the decision. Upstream read rules (e.g. resolving cases where a lang key doesn't match the id) live in the generator (scripts/gen-blocks.mjs) — only intentional overrides that deliberately diverge from upstream's presentation belong here. Slabs and stairs are derived from their base material, so they're not written individually (the mapping is in scripts/materials-with-variants.mjs).",
